  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "t14_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          -700
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## Name it once, use it everywhere\n\nThe **Variables** node declares three names. Every `${...}` below reads from\nit \u2014 the filter's query, the chart's title, the card's caption.\n\nChange `region` to `South` in the Variables node and press **F5**: the\nfilter, the chart and the card all follow. Nothing else was edited.\n\n**A `${name}` is a real edge in the graph**, not a lookup \u2014 that is what\nmakes the re-run correct. Everything reading a variable is downstream of the\nnode that declares it, so it re-runs when the value changes and its cached\nresult is thrown away with it. Hold **Q** and you will see no wire, because\nthe dependency is derived from the text, not drawn.\n\n**Try it from a scheduler.** The same file, once per region, nothing edited:\n\n    python -m flograph.engine.headless 14_flow_variables.flograph --var region=South\n\nA name the flow doesn't declare stops the run rather than being ignored.\n\nSecrets work the same way but live outside the project: `${env:API_KEY}`\nreads from the .env file you point at under *Tools > Secrets\u2026*, so a\npassword never enters the .flograph you send someone.\n\n(A Note's own text is never substituted \u2014 otherwise this note would be\nasking for a variable called `env:API_KEY` and stopping the run.)\n",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 560
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null,
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
        "locked": false,
        "frozen": false,
        "frozen_fingerprint": null,
        "exclusive": null,
        "preview": true,
        "port_labels": null,
        "flow_pins": null,
        "ports_collapsed": false,
        "color": null,
        "compact_view": null,
        "mark": "",
        "mark_text": "",
        "mark_image": "",
        "z": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "t14_vars",
        "type": "flograph.util.variables",
        "pos": [
          0,
          0
        ],
        "params": {
          "assignments": "# name = value, one per line\nregion = North\nmin_units = 20\nchart_title = Units by month\n",
          "table_mode": "first row (columns are names)"
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": "Settings",
        "description": "",
        "active": true,
